---
description: Avoid common AI coding mistakes
alwaysApply: true
---

- Do not rewrite working code without a reason.
- Do not create new files when an existing file is appropriate.
- Do not introduce a new dependency without checking existing dependencies first.
- Do not change public APIs unless required.
- Do not change database schemas without explicit confirmation.
- Do not remove tests to make the build pass.
- Do not silently change behavior to satisfy a test.
- Do not add unnecessary comments explaining obvious code.
- Do not refactor unrelated code.
- Do not claim something works without verifying it.
